          swc({q:"A café had 5 customers on its first day and 40 customers on a later day. How many times as many customers did it have later?",state:"We need the number of five-customer groups in 40.",steps:["'Times as many' asks how many groups of 5 fit into 40.","Divide larger by smaller: 40 ÷ 5 = 8."],answer:"It had 8 times as many customers.",conclusion:"It had eight times as many customers",check:"5 × 8 = 40.",structureId:"multiplicative_factor_basic",difficulty:1}),
          swc({q:"A tree was 4 m tall and is now 28 m tall. How many times as tall is it now?",state:"Both heights use metres, so division can compare their scale directly.",steps:["Both heights share the same unit, so divide the later height by the earlier one.","28 ÷ 4 = 7."],answer:"The tree is 7 times as tall.",conclusion:"The tree is seven times as tall",check:"4 m × 7 = 28 m.",structureId:"multiplicative_factor_basic",difficulty:2}),
          swc({q:"A library began with 6 books and later had 198. How many times as many books did it have later?",state:"The scale factor counts how many groups of 6 make 198.",steps:["Use 6 × 30 = 180, leaving 18.","18 contains three more groups of 6.","Therefore, 198 ÷ 6 = 33."],answer:"It had 33 times as many books.",conclusion:"It had 33 times as many books",check:"6 × 33 = 198.",structureId:"multiplicative_factor_basic",difficulty:2}),
          clear({q:"A model car is 12 cm long. A real car is 432 cm long. How many times as long is the real car, and what length would a model of a 504 cm van have at the same scale?",state:"First find the real-to-model scale factor, then reverse that relationship for the van model.",comprehend:"The same scale factor connects every model length to its matching real length.",link:"Divide real by model to find the factor. Then divide the van's real length by that factor to shrink it to model size.",explain:"Calculate the scale, apply it in reverse to 504 cm and check both relationships.",steps:["Scale factor: 432 ÷ 12 = 36.","Van model length: 504 ÷ 36 = 14 cm."],answer:"The real car is 36 times as long, and the van model would be 14 cm long.",conclusion:"The scale factor is 36 and the van model is 14 cm long",check:"12 × 36 = 432 and 14 × 36 = 504.",review:"Both real lengths are 36 times their model lengths, so the scale has been used consistently.",structureId:"multiplicative_factor_basic",difficulty:2})
